  "text": "Across the terrace, an alto saxophone climbed above the crowd. A small group from the Marching Herons was performing beside the radio booth. The saxophonist played with his eyes half closed, then opened them at the exact moment Nia stepped closer. After the set, he introduced himself as Julian Cross, second-year media arts student, campus radio host, and, according to him, occasional rescuer of boring events. This event was not boring, Nia said. Then I can take the night off. His confidence should have been irritating. Somehow, it was not.",
